819e150d27e" 13194139534838 true] [17592186313711 1145 "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nFirst, we rewrite the sequence in the form ${a}_{n}=a\\cdot {r}^{n},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{{5}^{n+1}}{{x}^{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot {5}^{n}}{{x}^{n}} \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{{5}^{n}}{{x}^{n}} \\\\  & =5{(\\frac{5}{x})}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe see that this is a geometric sequence with the common ratio $r=\\frac{5}{x}.$ Since $x$ is positive,  $r$ is also positive. So, the convergence condition is $0<r\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, the  sequence converges for \n\n$$\n0<\\frac{5}{x}\\le 1\\,⟹\\,x\\ge 5.\n$$" 13194139534838 true] [17592186313712 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313713 13194139534838 true] [17592186313712 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534838 true] [17592186313712 1041 "field-1" 13194139534838 true] [17592186313712 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313713 13194139534838 true] [17592186313712 1110 #uuid "e7665fa5-9555-5d76-96b9-b1d9f4ac714a" 13194139534838 true] [17592186313713 1034 "\\ge" 13194139534838 true] [17592186313713 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534838 true] [17592186313713 1111 #uuid "981b5ffa-a0d4-5990-a936-459652f1649b" 13194139534838 true] [17592186313714 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313715 13194139534838 true] [17592186313714 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534838 true] [17592186313714 1041 "field-2" 13194139534838 true] [17592186313714 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313715 13194139534838 true] [17592186313714 1110 #uuid "d95d1ccd-88ba-51fb-ae00-5a93ba3739e9" 13194139534838 true] [17592186313715 1034 "5" 13194139534838 true] [17592186313715 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534838 true] [17592186313715 1111 #uuid "8225eb13-4cd4-5e81-ba79-8ee1fc4bff50" 13194139534838 true] [17592186313716 1017 #edb/ref 17592186313717 13194139534838 true] [17592186313716 1089 "q-49570" 13194139534838 true] [17592186313716 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534838 true] [17592186313716 1100 "Consider the sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{x}^{n+3}}{{3}^{n}\\cdot x},$ where $x$ is a positive real number and $n\\ge 1.$ What are the values of $x$ for which the sequence converges?" 13194139534838 true] [17592186313716 1113 #uuid "6fc238f8-0118-5614-b187-86df412902ed" 13194139534838 true] [17592186313716 1145 "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nFirst, we rewrite the sequence in the form ${a}_{n}=a\\cdot {r}^{n},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{{x}^{n+3}}{{3}^{n}\\cdot x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{n}\\cdot {x}^{3}}{{3}^{n}\\cdot x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\frac{x}{3})}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe see that this is a geometric sequence with the common ratio $r=\\frac{x}{3}.$ Since $x$ is positive,  $r$ is also positive. So, the convergence condition is $0<r\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, the  sequence converges for \n\n$$\n0<\\frac{x}{3}\\le 1\\,⟹\\,0<x\\le 3.\n$$" 13194139534838 true] [17592186313717 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313718 13194139534838 true] [17592186313717 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313719 13194139534838 true] [17592186313717 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313720 13194139534838 true] [17592186313717 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313721 13194139534838 true] [17592186313717 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313722 13194139534838 true] [17592186313717 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534838 true] [